{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GCTHMxskX4dKXxabnXVjyg","type":"tool_result","content":"# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n./internal/agent/claude/real_test.go:118:\t\t\t\tif !r.OK || r.Subtype != \"success\" || r.CostUSD == nil || r.LimitHit != nil || r.CLIVersion != TestedVersion || r.SessionID != \"session-1\" {\n./internal/agent/claude/cli_integration_test.go:5:// them on every TestedVersion bump (including the OAuth token and API key\n./internal/agent/claude/cli_integration_test.go:461:// docs/proposal.md, #125), but re-check it on a TestedVersion bump when the\n./internal/agent/claude/parse_test.go:6:// CLI (TestedVersion), made with the capture harness (capture_test.go, build\n./internal/agent/claude/adapter.go:12:// TestedVersion is the CLI release the flags and stream-json schema were\n./internal/agent/claude/adapter.go:14:const TestedVersion = \"2.1.330\"\n./internal/agent/claude/cli_scripted_integration_test.go:9:// them on every TestedVersion bump.\n./internal/agent/claude/capture_test.go:90:\tif err != nil || !strings.Contains(string(ver), TestedVersion) {\n./internal/agent/claude/capture_test.go:91:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"claude --version = %q (%v), want %s: a capture from another release does not match the adapter\", ver, err, TestedVersion)\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Builds the root Dockerfile and checks the image:\n#   - one build for linux/amd64 + linux/arm64 into an OCI layout: the index lists exactly those two platforms\n#   - the native platform loaded into Docker: ard version, the tools at their pinned versions, uid, labels,\n#     and the cve scanner run in the image as a plain subprocess (how `ard serve` runs it in a container)\n# Needs Docker with buildx and network (base image, module proxy, osv.dev). Prints PASS:/FAIL: per case.\n# Exit 0 ok, 1 a case failed, 2 tooling.\nset -uo pipefail\n\nROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nBUILDER=\"${ARD_IMAGE_TEST_BUILDER:-ard-image-test}\"\ncommand -v docker >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"ERROR: docker is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\ndocker buildx version >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"ERROR: docker buildx is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\ncommand -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"ERROR: jq is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\nwork=\"$(mktemp -d)\" || { echo \"ERROR: mktemp failed\" >&2; exit 2; }\ntag=\"ard-image-test:$$\"\ntag2=\"ard-image-test:$$-v\"\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$work\"; docker image rm -f \"$tag\" \"$tag2\" >/dev/null 2>&1' EXIT\nfailures=0\npass() { echo \"PASS: $1\"; }\nfail() { echo \"FAIL: $1${2:+ - $2}\" >&2; failures=$((failures + 1)); }\n\ndocker buildx inspect \"$BUILDER\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || docker buildx create --name \"$BUILDER\" --driver docker-container >/dev/null \\\n  || { echo \"ERROR: cannot create buildx builder $BUILDER\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\nversion=\"$(git -C \"$ROOT\" describe --tags --always)\"\nrevision=\"$(git -C \"$ROOT\" rev-parse HEAD)\"\ncase \"$(docker info --format '{{.Architecture}}')\" in\n  aarch64|arm64) native=linux/arm64 ;;\n## Delivery\n\nHow ard itself is built, published and deployed. Jenkins and Argo CD do the work; the cluster-specific wiring (the Jenkins job definitions and their publishing Jenkinsfiles, credentials, the Argo CD projects and the image pin) lives in the deployment repository, not here. This repository holds only what is ard's: the `Makefile` targets CI runs, `Dockerfile`, `deploy/` and `deploy/cosign.pub`, the key ard images are signed with. `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`, `deploy/` and any `Jenkinsfile*` are in ard's `merge.protected_paths`, so the merger never lands a change to them without a human approva\n\n- **Checks.** The Jenkins multibranch job `ard-ci` builds every same-repository branch and pull request, `worker/*` branches included, but never forks, with `make lint`, `make test`, `make build` and `make chart-test`. Its pipeline is loaded from the deployment repository, never from the branch, so branch code supplies only those targets and runs in a pod with no credential and no service account token. `main` requires both its status, `continuous-integration/jenkins/pr-merge`, and the Actions `test` job ([#219](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/219)): Jenkins stops reporting to a PR \n- **Publish.** A green `main` build starts `ard-build`, whose Jenkinsfile is not in this repository, so nothing merged here can reach its credentials. It builds the `Dockerfile` for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` (no emulation: every `RUN` cross-compiles or downloads on the build platform), signs the digest with cosign, and pushes `ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard:sha-<7>` (never re-pushed) and `:main`.\n- **Deploy.** A deploy job verifies the signature and the revision label, checks the new commit descends from the pinned one, and pins the digest and commit in the deployment repository. Argo CD renders this repository's `deploy/argocd` chart (the app of apps) with that pin and the site's values: one child Application per target repository, named `ard-<instance>`, reading `deploy/charts/ard-serve` at the pinned commit, so chart and image move together. The cluster admits no other Application from that chart.\n- **Release.** An annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` (`git tag -a`) builds that commit with `VERSION=vX.Y.Z`, pushes `:vX.Y.Z` and moves `:latest` when it is the highest version. Release tags are annotated because Jenkins builds only tags at most a day old and dates a lightweight tag by its commit, so a lightweight tag on an older commit never builds. Releases do not change what is deployed, which follows `main`.\n- **Kill switch in a cluster.** `kubectl -n <namespace> exec deploy/ard-<instance> -- touch /home/ard/.ard/pause/<owner>/<repo>` pauses `ard serve`; `rm` resumes.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6629f6eb-a30e-4bf7-a39c-365e453abc49","uuid":"6eafd3b3-0ca2-45df-bc34-143fc65d4eeb","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:13:03.103Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n./internal/agent/claude/real_test.go:118:\t\t\t\tif !r.OK || r.Subtype != \"success\" || r.CostUSD == nil || r.LimitHit != nil || r.CLIVersion != TestedVersion || r.SessionID != \"session-1\" {\n./internal/agent/claude/cli_integration_test.go:5:// them on every TestedVersion bump (including the OAuth token and API key\n./internal/agent/claude/cli_integration_test.go:461:// docs/proposal.md, #125), but re-check it on a TestedVersion bump when the\n./internal/agent/claude/parse_test.go:6:// CLI (TestedVersion), made with the capture harness (capture_test.go, build\n./internal/agent/claude/adapter.go:12:// TestedVersion is the CLI release the flags and stream-json schema were\n./internal/agent/claude/adapter.go:14:const TestedVersion = \"2.1.330\"\n./internal/agent/claude/cli_scripted_integration_test.go:9:// them on every TestedVersion bump.\n./internal/agent/claude/capture_test.go:90:\t