{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0133pueutazcBVFhFuTUujps","type":"tool_result","content":"# ard controller image: the static ard binary plus the cve scanner's tools, so\n# `ard serve` in a container can run the cve role as a host subprocess.\n# Published as ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard.\n#\n# Builds for both platforms on a host without QEMU/binfmt: every RUN is in a\n# stage on $BUILDPLATFORM (Go cross-compiles, per-arch binaries are downloaded\n# with checksums), and the final stage only copies files in.\n#\n# The base is trixie, not bookworm: git 2.39 breaks the committer's fetches (#163).\n#\n# Tool versions and checksums are the cve scanner's\n# (internal/roles/scanners/cve/Dockerfile); keep them in step.\n#\n#   docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64 \\\n#     --build-arg VERSION=$(git describe --tags --always) \\\n#     --build-arg REVISION=$(git rev-parse HEAD) .\n\nARG GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.4-trixie@sha256:f18c3d73a184fb0582828510722e723b63a93f7188d11dd223d9be6f6880e65d\n\nFROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM ${GO_IMAGE} AS build\nARG TARGETOS\nARG TARGETARCH\nARG VERSION=dev\nARG GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.10.0\nWORKDIR /src\nCOPY go.mod go.sum ./\nRUN go mod download\nCOPY . .\nRUN mkdir -p /out && \\\n    CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=${TARGETOS} GOARCH=${TARGETARCH} \\\n    go build -trimpath -ldflags \"-s -w -X main.version=${VERSION}\" -o /out/ard ./cmd/ard\n# A cross-compiled `go install` lands in bin/<os>_<arch>/, a native one in bin/.\nRUN set -eu; \\\n    CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=${TARGETOS} GOARCH=${TARGETARCH} \\\n      go install golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@${GOVULNCHECK_VERSION}; \\\n    gopath=\"$(go env GOPATH)\"; f=\"${gopath}/bin/${TARGETOS}_${TARGETARCH}/govulncheck\"; \\\n    [ -f \"$f\" ] || f=\"${gopath}/bin/govulncheck\"; \\\n    cp \"$f\" /out/govulncheck\n\nFROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM ${GO_IMAGE} AS tools\nARG TARGETARCH\nARG OSV_SCANNER_VERSION=v2.7.1\nARG OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_AMD64=fb7dab19a8bd9bbe5c3189f09d4b7ee1820c9553a23bac202648a56efd2f6ee8\nARG OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_ARM64=983d22fbad9724514e3fcc6acc83b5fa64c5ffa6b0d9f510028f22c1b223ff81\nARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\nARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\nARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\n# tini v0.19.0 static, checksums from the release's .sha256sum files.\nARG TINI_VERSION=v0.19.0\nARG TINI_SHA256_AMD64=c5b0666b4cb676901f90dfcb37106783c5fe2077b04590973b885950611b30ee\nARG TINI_SHA256_ARM64=eae1d3aa50c48fb23b8cbdf4e369d0910dfc538566bfd09df89a774aa84a48b9\nRUN set -eu; \\\n    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n      amd64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_AMD64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\"; tini_sha=\"${TINI_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n      arm64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_ARM64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\"; tini_sha=\"${TINI_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n    esac; \\\n    mkdir /out; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/osv-scanner \"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/releases/download/${OSV_SCANNER_VERSION}/osv-scanner_linux_${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${osv_sha}  /out/osv-scanner\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/tini \"https://github.com/krallin/tini/releases/download/${TINI_VERSION}/tini-static-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${tini_sha}  /out/tini\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    chmod 0755 /out/osv-scanner /out/jq /out/tini\n\n# The final image keeps the Go toolchain (govulncheck loads packages with it);\n# git and ca-certificates are already in the golang image.\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE}\nARG VERSION=dev\n// Package claude adapts the Claude Code CLI (`claude -p`).\npackage claude\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/agent\"\n)\n\n// TestedVersion is the CLI release the flags and stream-json schema were\n// verified against. Callers warn when a run reports another version.\nconst TestedVersion = \"2.1.330\"\n\n// Options configures New.\ntype Options struct{ Binary string } // default \"claude\"\n\n// Adapter implements agent.Adapter for Claude Code.\ntype Adapter struct{ binary string }\n\n// New returns an adapter.\nfunc New(o Options) *Adapter {\n\tif o.Binary == \"\" {\n\t\to.Binary = \"claude\"\n\t}\n\treturn &Adapter{binary: o.Binary}\n}\n\n// Name is the value of the config's agent key.\n287:| Runtime | the role's `Dockerfile` image under Docker if it has one, else a host subprocess; hard timeout | a pod from the role's `Dockerfile` image, or the default `ard-agent` image; hard timeou\n328:**The starter worker (`workers/engineer`, #34).** `.ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt` implements `plan.md`'s `## Implementation`. Its inputs, all untrusted, are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md` and `\n407:- A `Dockerfile` builds the role's image; without one the local executor runs a host subprocess and the Kubernetes executor uses the default `ard-agent` image (agent CLIs, git, common linters). A \nConfiguration is by convention: a role exists because its directory exists, and `.ard/config.yaml` holds only global settings and overrides. No prompt path is written anywhere; ard reads `.ard/<type>/<name>/prompt.txt`. Model credentials are host settings (`ARD_AGENT_AUTH`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLA\n\n```\n.ard/\n├── config.yaml          # global settings and overrides only\n├── scanners/<name>/     # scan (executable) or prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── triage/<name>/       # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\nadapter.go\nadapter_test.go\ncapture_test.go\ncli_integration_test.go\ncli_scripted_integration_test.go\nlimit_parse_test.go\nparse.go\nparse_test.go\nprompt.go\nreal_test.go\nscrub_test.go\ntestdata\nwindows_test.go","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"ses